WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first-star idol!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.520
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.620
Yume-chan.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.580
Yume-chan!

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.710
Koharu-chan!

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.720
I bet you were basking in the glow of your victory. {I really tried to avoid afterglow}

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:34.590
You could tell?

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.220
Everything shows on your face, Yume-chan.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.350
Well, I can tell what you're thinking too.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.220
Huh?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:46.230
You want to let even more people shine through Rainbow Berry Parfait, right?

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.230
You got it!

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.570
So, about that design we were talking about...

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.610
Oh, I came up with a few ideas too...

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.450
We need to raise our Aikatsu Ranking like Yume.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.620
Have any plans, Rola?

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:05.960
Yeah.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.210
I'm going to go for this show.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.090
"Amazing Idol Fes". {for consistency this ep}

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.550
That's the last big event of the year, isn't it?

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:24.520
Yeah. With my current rank, my only chance at the Final Tournament is winning this.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.060
That's why...

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.270
I'm going to put it all on the line here.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.660
Now we're ready!

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.290
What are these?

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.670
A Japanese lucky item you use when you wanna get serious!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.300
Ako-chan told me about it!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.550
It's lovely!

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.050
We're gonna make it into the Final Tournament!

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.300
Osu!

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.890
What does that mean?

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.640
It's a miracle word that makes you braver!

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.730
I got this from Ako-chan too!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.310
That's very wonderful!

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.940
Let's get serious!

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.400
Osu!

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:35.820
Osu!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.110
Osu!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.740
<i>The Sun Dress.</i>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.500
<i>I have the same genes as Mother... {that's not how it works!}</i>

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.290
<i>So why is it?</i>

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.800
<i>Why won't the Sun Dress come to me?</i>

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.800
<i>What am I missing?</i>

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:10.310
Rei...

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.560
Hello.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.940
Hey, Elza. Sorry to bother you.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:22.530
I'm watching over Kirara and Aria training for the Final Tournament right now.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.530
One, two, three, four!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.570
Won't you come give them a word of advice?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.570
Two, two, three—

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.540
If you think they need it, Rei, then you speak with them.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.790
No, I really think it would benefit them more if you—

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.330
Was I not clear?

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.250
Huh?

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.340
I <i>told</i> you to handle it yourself.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.210
But!

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:40.510
<b>Kizaki Rei</b>

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.380
Elza!

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.390
Elza...

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.850
The Final Tournament...

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:57.270
For me to keep a firm grip on first...

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.780
The Amazing Idol Fes?

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.030
Yeah, I'm thinking of entering.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.410
That's great! I know you'll be able to bring it home.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.030
I was hoping you'd say that.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:14.830
To get the result I want, I have to Aikatsu with everything I've got.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:15.960
Yep!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.120
Rola!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.130
This is bad, Rola!

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:19.750
Eh?

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.210
What's wrong?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.300
E-Elza-san is...

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.800
Elza-san is entering the Amazing Idol Fes too!

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.680
Rola, did you apply already?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.890
Not yet...

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:33.930
Rola.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:41.690
If I enter the Fes as I am now...
I have no chance of beating Elza-san.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.190
But this is your last chance to make the Final Tournament...

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.320
I know that!

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.070
But...

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.990
How else do you intend to make it?

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:02.130
And after that, none of you were able to say anything to Rola?

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.760
I mean, if she doesn't win, there goes any hope of being in the Final Tournament.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:12.310
At the same time, she'll have even less of a chance of being in the Finals if she doesn't try.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:14.560
That may be true...

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:19.730
In the end, I think the most important thing is how Rola feels about it.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.190
What do you mean?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:29.160
Knowing Rola, she should be able to find the answer that's right for her.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:33.530
And I want to support her decision all the way.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.060
<i>Even if I were to enter the Fes,</i>

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.400
<i>I'd still have to beat Elza-san to win.</i>

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.820
<i>What now... What should I do?</i>

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.410
<i>Somebody's keeping pace with me.</i>

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.330
That gets me going! {yay for literal use}

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.670
<i>That should be enough...</i>

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.510
<i>She's still there!</i>

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.130
<i>If I lose here...</i>

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.760
<i>I get the feeling I'll end up losing everything!</i>

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:41.690
I'm not gonna lose!

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.020
No way!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.660
Wh-Why... are you chasing me?

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.950
I-I'm sorry...

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.160
Whenever I see someone in front of me,
 I get the urge to pass them.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.330
Guess it's my personality.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.460
Personality?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.380
But yeah, I can't stand losing to anyone myself.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.680
Maybe it's my personality?

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.770
I'm Maekawa Ayano. Nice to meet you.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.520
I'm Sakuraba Rola. Likewise.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.860
Huh? You're a marathon runner?

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:30.860
Yeah.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.650
I'm one of our team's representatives too.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.280
That's amazing.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:40.120
Uh, I'm pretty sure you're the amazing one for being able to keep up with me.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.500
I just didn't want to lose.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.620
Sounds like a competitive spirit.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:50.500
Yes, though thanks to that, I've had my share of painful experiences.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.170
It's the same for me.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.010
Huh?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:09:00.140
I said I was a representative of my team, 
but my times are the worst out of all of us.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.270
I come in last all the time.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.770
Actually, we have a really big meet coming up. {sugggggoku!}

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:11.650
And if I don't get any results there, I'll probably get cut.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:20.030
My coach said that since the competition will be strong, I'll have a hard time placing well with my times.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.620
Does that mean you'll wait and enter a different meet?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.120
No, I decided to enter.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:26.830
{this doesn't must, does it?}{sure if you [don't] want}

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.000
This isn't the only match I'll have.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.760
I want to keep doing marathons in the future, so I intentionally chose not to run away.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.510
I hate losing, just like you.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.510
I don't want to lose to my weaker self.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.270
Your weaker self...

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.770
Man, I'm really bad at acting cool.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.730
Not at all!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.860
Thank you so much, Ayano-san!

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.610
Did I do something?

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:53.860
Yes!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.610
Then I'm glad.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.780
I should get going soon.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.080
Sure. See you later.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.460
Oh, also!

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:11.380
To tell you the truth, I'm an idol!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.510
Yeah... I knew.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.640
Thanks for waiting, Yume!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.600
Rola, what did you need so late at night?

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.020
I've decided to enter.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:30.600
Huh?

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.860
I'm going to hit Elza-san with everything I've got.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.740
Good! I knew that's what you'd say.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:45.620
Okay! Now that you're in, I'm going to support you the best I can!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.120
Well, aren't you reliable! {too bad we didn't give her a form that's more like "that gets you reliable"}

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:06.180
I've participated in tons of competitions, and lost and cried my fair share.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:12.100
But getting scared of losing and running away isn't like me.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.020
Yeah, that's right.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:21.320
Every time I lose, every time I cry, I feel myself growing stronger. {I don't care if it's a comma splice}

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:29.410
If I keep at it, little by little, I can say goodbye to my weaker self.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.130
You're not weak at all, Rola.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.470
Thanks. It's because I have you, Yume.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:44.720
No matter what happens, I swear I'll never run away again.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:46.470
Yeah.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.940
Everyone! {who the hell is this?}{!}

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:57.900
Welcome to the big idol event, the Amazing Idol Fes!

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.900
It's a dreamlike gathering of popular idols!

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.910
Enjoy yourselves to the very last song!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.160
It's starting.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.290
I'm more nervous for this than for my own shows.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:15.290
What's the point of <i>you</i> getting so worked up?

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:20.010
That said, Rola has shown such strong resolve.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.840
Yeah, she wants to win against herself.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.970
How very like her.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.220
Elza-sama!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.520
Osu!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.100
Osu!

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.310
Fight!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.100
Osu!

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.310
<i>Taking the stage all of a sudden...</i>

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.860
<i>What is going through your head?</i>

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.120
I won't run.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:49.370
This is to defeat my weaker self!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.660
It's <i>my</i> time to shine!

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:12.520
Come on, let's go down the path we believed in! {this is new}

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:14.920
Wow...

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.590
Her dress evolved.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.010
What was that?

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.010
How beautiful...

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:20.090
Wh-What is with that dress?

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:21.640
Isn't that...

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.010
The Sun... Dress.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.600
Now, nobody can ever compare to Elza-san.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:38.400
Elza-sama's wings are shining golden!

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.490
Lovely! It's too lovely!

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:44.660
Elza, it's finally yours!

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.120
The glorious Sun Dress!

00:19:53.630 --> 00:20:00.420
Here at Kira Kira Stadium, the annual big event Amazing Idol Fes has just concluded.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.180
I thought I understood...

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:06.260
but Elza-san really is incredible.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.100
You did your best, didn't you?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.020
That's why you shouldn't have any regrets.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.110
Still...

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.330
In the end...

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:32.250
It really hurts.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:37.250
Thank you for your comments. {see, even the background commentators skip a huge part of the interview}

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.130
Let's interview the next athlete here. {I would start the uncommented lines here, as in the CCs}

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:42.920
Maekawa Ayano, that was a close race.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:46.090
Thank you, but I won't let it end here.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:50.060
I will continue fighting as long as I'm a marathon runner.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:53.810
Is there some special method you use to think so positively?

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.810
Ayano-san.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:54.560
Yes.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:21:00.820
Actually, I really love the idol Sakuraba Rola-chan. Listening to her songs always cheers me up.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.490
You mean Rola-chan from Four Star Academy?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:04.570
That's her.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:10.580
The next time I see her, I'd like to tell her thank you in person.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.950
Thank you very much, Maekawa.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.040
We're looking forward to your next race.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.420
Thank you.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:26.590
Yume?

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.720
Looks like I lost.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:33.680
Yeah...

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.980
But this isn't the end.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.480
There will be much more in the future.

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.440
As long as I'm an idol.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.860
Yeah.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.160
Thanks, Yume.

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:51.740
I...

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.500
I'll become even stronger.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:57.250
Yeah.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.170
At last, I've done it!

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:06.880
I've obtained the legendary dress that only the chosen idol is permitted to wear!

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:11.010
I hold it in my hands!

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:14.520
Yes, for my name is Perfect Elza! {oh my god she's evil. she's lost her fucking mind}

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:18.230
I now stand upon the ultimate apex! {I'm tempted to sub the HA AHA HA HA HA HA}

00:23:55.950 --> 00:24:01.120
The Eternal Queen Coord is the legendary dress only the chosen idol may wear.

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:04.670
The red roses and gold crown motif are magnificent.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:06.460
It is truly perfect!

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.090
I've finally obtained the Sun Dress!

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:13.340
Let's heat up Christmas once again!

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:17.390
You bet! We'll make everyone's hearts beat out of their chests!

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:19.350
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:20.850
Thank You Merry X-mas! {how else to do merikuri?}{wasn't there something like this in kin-iro mosaic? I guess it could just be merry christmas}

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:23.440
Become the first-star idol!
